iative.\n\nReason: H9 creates an Open 3 (G8-H9-I10) along the diagonal. This is the strongest structure available as it offers two potential winning extensions (F7 and J11). White is forced to defend, giving Black the initiative. The other forcing moves (G5, L6) result in blocked 4s which are dead ends, whereas H9 opens up the board for a potential win.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "H", "row": 9}'}
